<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · Maritime Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Paser Sultanate</h1><p class="st-meta">1516 CE – 1906 CE (approx.) · capital Paser Belengkong</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Malay-Dayak sultanate in the southeast of East Kalimantan, ruled from Paser Belengkong until the Dutch took control in 1906.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Paser lay on the Kendilo River in southeast <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borneo">Borneo</a>, between the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/banjar-sultanate">Banjar Sultanate</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kutai-kartanegara-sultanate">Kutai Kartanegara</a>. Local tradition traces its royal house to Putri Petung, a princess born from a bamboo stem, who married a prince from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>. Its rulers adopted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> in the 16th century, and the register dates the sultanate from 1516.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Paser drew on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> farming and forest products such as rattan and resin, and traded with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banjarmasin">Banjarmasin</a> and with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bugis">Bugis</a> merchants, many of whom settled on its coast in the 18th century and gained influence at court. It acknowledged Banjar overlordship at times.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> made treaties with Paser in the 19th century and annexed it into their administration in 1906, leaving the sultan as a figurehead. Its lands became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paser-regency">Paser Regency</a>, and the old palace at Paser Belengkong is now a museum.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="sultanate, 1516 CE – 1906 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">sultanate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Maritime Southeast Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:89.87%;width:7.76%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1516 CE – 1906 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>sultanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Paser Belengkong</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Paser, Banjar Malay</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/indonesia">Indonesia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Pasir Sultanate, Sultanate of Paser</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1711&amp;focus=paser-sultanate" aria-label="Paser Sultanate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7907 2251 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Paser Sultanate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M8227 2507L7959 2663"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7959 2663h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8227 2507h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8227 2507h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Paser Belengkong. <a href="/atlas?year=1711&amp;focus=paser-sultanate">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

